// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Mover set-piece: measurement and proof surface for LARGE theatrical movers.
// See mover-setpiece.README.md for stations and waypoints.
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/mover-setpiece.map -o content/dev/maps/mover-setpiece.prl
// Layout, TrenchBroom units, 1 unit = 0.0254 m, floor top at z 0, ceiling at z 320.
// Arena: x 0 to 1280, y 0 to 1024. Back room: x 0 to 1280, y 1088 to 1600.
// Dividing wall y 1024 to 1088 with a 544 x 224 opening at x 96 to 640 and a
// door pocket at x 640 to 1184, y 1040 to 1072, z 0 to 224.
// Rising-room shaft under the arena floor: hole x 832 to 1152, y 160 to 480,
// shaft floor top at z -192.
// Hallway: a 128 x 160 mouth in the arena east wall at y 640 to 768, z 0 to 160.
// Leg 1 runs east to x 1792, leg 2 runs north over y 768 to 1136, x 1664 to 1792,
// into the lift chamber through a 128 x 160 opening in its south wall.
// Lift chamber: x 1344 to 2112, y 1152 to 1984, z 0 to 320.
// Big rising-room shaft in the chamber floor: hole x 1472 to 1984, y 1296 to 1856,
// shaft floor top at z -336. The big room is 512 x 560 outside with 64 thick walls
// and slabs; lowered, its roof top sits 48 below the chamber floor. Its south wall
// has a round-arch doorway 100 wide, x 1678 to 1778, apex 130 above the room floor.
// Hallway and chamber lights are four baked spots and two dim baked point lights.
// Every brush is convex. All are axis-aligned boxes except the ten arch voussoirs,
// prisms whose lower faces follow the arch. Keep comments free of braces and quotes.
